{"node":{"id":"MONDO:0007057","label":"acroosteolysis dominant type","definition":"A rare genetic osteolysis syndrome resulting from protein-truncating variants in exon 34 of the NOTCH2 gene. These variants disrupt only the PEST domain, escape nonsense-mediated decay, and are postulated to function through a gain-of-function mechanism. This condition is characterized by acroosteolysis of distal phalanges and generalized osteoporosis, associated with additional ossification anomalies, craniofacial dysmorphism, dental anomalies and a wide range of other characteristics. Hearing loss, renal cysts, and cardiovascular anomalies are variably present.","synonyms":["Arthrodentoosteodysplasia","Cheney syndrome","HJCYS","Hajdu Cheney Syndrome","Hajdu-Cheney syndrome","Hajdu-Cheney syndrome-NOTCH2","acrodentoosteodysplasia","acroosteolysis with osteoporosis and changes in skull and mandible"],"xrefs":["DOID:2736","GARD:0000508","ICD9:756.59","MEDGEN:182961","MESH:C531695","MESH:C535663","MESH:C537586","NCIT:C84745","NORD:1214","OMIM:102500","Orphanet:955","SCTID:63122002","UMLS:C0917715"],"parents":[],"parents_labels":{},"children":[],"children_labels":{},"in_core":false,"cluster_id":1,"is_group":false,"n_genes":1,"n_phenotypes":112,"mechanism_classes":[]},"genes":[{"id":"e_69e35710cf9b","source":"MONDO:0007057","target":"NOTCH2","type":"caused_by","evidence":[{"db":"Orphanet","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:955","level":"curated","date":"2026-06-23","url":"https://www.orpha.net/en/disease/detail/955","confidence":0.95,"snippet":"Disease-causing germline mutation(s) (gain of function) in (Assessed) — notch receptor 2"},{"db":"HPO","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:955","level":"curated","date":"2026-09-02","confidence":0.9,"url":"https://hpo.jax.org/browse/disease/ORPHA:955","snippet":"NOTCH2 is annotated as disease gene of ORPHA:955 (HPO genes_to_phenotype, Orphanet-derived)"}],"contradicting":[],"confidence":0.95,"independent_sources":["Orphanet"],"level":"curated"}],"